      Special-Event Park-and-Ride Planning Problem
      CEE 6410/5410
      David Rosenberg
      October 10, 2026
       
      This problem was contributed by Dr. Ran Sun and expanded by Dr. David Rosenberg
       
      Learning objectives.
      Students will be able to:
      •   Define dimensions, decision variables and an objective function;
      •   Formulate demand, capacity, and service-quality constraints;
      •   Solve a small linear program;
      •   Identify constraints;
       
      Problem Statement
      State Department of Transportation guidance for special events emphasizes advance parklotanning for transportation demand, traffic, parking, transit operations, and seating.
       
      Passengers must also be assigned in full bus-loads of 50 passengers per bus.
       
      Additionally, the event parklotanners must rent and bring in grandstands for the attendees. They have 2 potential venders. Each vender has an up-front reservation cost, number of seats per grandstand, and cost to load, ship, and setup a grandstand.
       
      Vendor  Reservation cost ($)    Seats per grandstand    Cost to load, ship, and setup ($ per grandstand)
      PurpleRain $1,000                   100                 200
      Blue Sky    $1,500                  200                 300
       
      Full details at https://usu.instructure.com/courses/818402/files/100525844?wrap=1
       
      David E Rosenberg
      david.rosenberg@usu.edu
  32   
  33  * 1. DEFINE the SETS
  34  SETS parklot Parking Lots /north, south, west/
  35      vendor Vendors of grandstands /PurpleRain, BlueSky/;
  36   
  37  * 2. DEFINE input data
  38  PARAMETERS
  39     MaxPassengers(parklot) maximimum number of peoparklote parking lot can handle (Number)
  40           /north 600,
  41            south 500,
  42            west  600/
  43     Cost(parklot) cost per passenger from parking lot ($ per person)
  44            /north 4,
  45            south 5,
  46            west  7/
  47     TravelTime(parklot) Travel time from parking lot (minutes)
  48           /north 20,
  49            south 12,
  50            west  8/
  51     MaxAverageTime Maximum average travel time for all pasengers (minutes) /13/
  52     Attendees number of attendees /1200/
  53     ReservationCost(vendor) Cost to reserve grandstands from vendor ($)
  54          /PurpleRain 1000,
  55           BlueSky    1500/
  56     Seats(vendor) Seats per grandstand (number)
  57          /PurpleRain 100,
  58           BlueSky    200/
  59      UnitCost(vendor) Cost per grandstand to load ship and setup ($ per grandstand)
  60          /PurpleRain 200,
  61           BlueSky    300/
  62      Bus_load The amount of passengers per bus /50/;
  63   
  64   
  65   
  66  * 3. DEFINE the variables
  67  Variables
  68  TCOST the total cost of vendors and buses
  69  Buses(parklot) how many buses to schedule from each parking lot
  70  Grandstands(vendor) How many grandstands to schedule from vendor
  71  I(vendor) Binary decision variable to decide on which vendor;
  72   
  73  * Setting binary constraint for vendor
  74  Binary Variable
  75  I(vendor);
  76   
  77  * Setting Buses and Grandstands to be integers because you can't have 1/2 a bus or grandstand
  78  Integer Variables
  79  Buses(parklot)
  80  Grandstands(vendor);
  81   
  82   
  83  * 4. COMBINE variables and data in equations
  84  EQUATIONS
  85  Obj_func Objective function Equation
  86  Seat_Attendees_cons Ensure enough grandstand seats for all attendees
  87  Bus_attendees_cons Attendees constraint
  88  Capacity_cons(parklot) Capacity of parking facilities
  89  Travel_time_cons Constraint of max travel time per person;
  90   
  91  Obj_func.. TCOST =E= sum(parklot, Cost(parklot)*Buses(parklot)*Bus_load) +
  92                       sum(vendor, ReservationCost(vendor)*I(vendor) +
  93                       UnitCost(Vendor)*Grandstands(vendor));
  94   
  95  Seat_attendees_cons.. sum(vendor, I(vendor)*Seats(vendor)*Grandstands(vendor)) =G= Attendees;
  96  Bus_attendees_cons.. sum(parklot, Buses(parklot)*50) =G= Attendees;
  97  Capacity_cons(parklot).. Buses(parklot)*Bus_load =L= MaxPassengers(parklot);
  98  Travel_time_cons.. sum(parklot, Buses(parklot)*Bus_load*TravelTime(parklot)) =L=
  99                     MaxAverageTime * sum(parklot, Buses(parklot)*Bus_load);
 100   
 101   
 102  * 5. DEFINE the MODEL from the EQUATIONS
 103  Model Event /ALL/;
 104   
 105  * 6. Solve the Model as a Mixed Integer Program
 106  Solve Event using MIP minimizing TCOST;
